about_role:
Manage and support Sasol’s Socio-Economic Development and Corporate Social Investment programme (CSI) in South Africa through CSI programme execution which includes cost, quality and schedule control for all regions including enablement of the planning processes. Appointment and management of Implementation Partners identified for the execution of CSI programmes in line with Sasol’s Supply Chain and governance processes within the following focus areas:
Quality Healthcare;
Services Infrastructure;
Safety and Security;
Sasol for Good
Facilitate the implementation of a one Sasol South African cohesive integrated approach for community development, which includes health, infrastructure, environment and Sasol for Good projects, programmes and campaigns while ensuring the projects and programmes are linked to the strategic focus areas and address the findings and recommendation of the various studies conducted.
Engagement and alignment with all CSI regional managers to develop an integrated, standardised approach for selection and implementation of community development and Sasol for Good projects, programmes and campaigns.
Monitoring and evaluation frameworks and measures to ensure projects, programmes and campaigns are implemented according to the applicable plan and achieve the desired impact, managing data collection, analysis and reporting.

responsibilities:
Participate in the auditing, optimisation and implementation of an integrated water quality management system for the entire water supply chain (catchment, production, bulk and retail distribution), incorporating and applying the principles of international water safety planning. These aspects will include, but are not limited to:
Water quality guidelines and standards;
Water quality monitoring programmes;
Water quality risk registers; and
Water quality management procedures and incident protocols.
Identify legal requirements and plan compliance measures, taking cognisance of the Water Services Act and related regulations, the National Water Act, SANS 241, Blue Drop requirements, the National Water Resource Strategy and other applicable frameworks.
